# Settings app

Mirror macOS System Settings: sidebar search + account row + coloured icon list; detail pane with back/forward + title.

## Structure

- Entry: `src/applications/Settings.tsx` (`titleBar = true`, ~780×620)
- Shell/nav: `src/applications/settings/SettingsApp.tsx`
- Nav list: `src/applications/settings/nav.ts` (`SETTINGS_NAV`)
- Real pane: `AppearancePane.tsx` — stub others via `StubPane` / `GeneralPane`

## Patterns

- Traffic lights live in the sidebar (`AppActions` + `data-handle`), not a separate titlebar
- Selected nav item uses `background: var(--macos-accent)` + white label
- Grouped rows: rounded `[10px]` container, `var(--settings-group)`, hairline dividers
- Prefer existing shadcn `Switch` / `Select` / `RadioGroup` / `Input` styled as macOS
- New panes: add to `SETTINGS_NAV`, then branch in `SettingsApp` content area (implement or stub)
- Appearance changes go through `useTheme().updateTheme` only
